  "provenance": "ai-executed",
  "scope": "Real COCO photographs, 64\u00d764 center crops. The existing output generator was trained on 1,024 photos; 256 test photos are held out from this continuation. The photo is seen twice, then removed; the generated output receives only the agent workspace and noise. This tests still-image recall, not arbitrary text-to-image generation or real video. Encoder, state/memory and codec were frozen. Reset image MSE changed from 0.09674 to 0.05867 (39.4% lower); trained recall PSNR is 12.73 dB, versus 30.92 dB for direct codec reconstruction. The codec control receives the original image and transports within-patch detail; it is not compact semantic memory. In the first eight fixed test examples, training removes the synthetic square pattern but outputs remain mostly coarse color fields; the photographed objects are not reconstructed. Passing the declared optimization/context screens does not establish detailed or general photographic generation. A single training seed and fixed pair-shared sampling noise were used. Prior upstream COCO exposure limits the holdout claim.",
